    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag, a read-derived soft warning on owner responses that turns `true` when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard per-city cap of 50), while leaving the existing hard rejection at 50 untouched.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `capacityWarning` boolean read-only property to the owner schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec, giving it a setter).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ignore = true)` so MapStruct leaves the controller-derived field alone, matching the pattern used for `bulkSignupWarning`.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40L` and a `capacityWarning(String city)` method returning `true` when `ownersInCity(city)` is in `[40, 50)`. It reuses the same `ownersInCity` counting the hard `rejectCityAtCapacity` check uses, so the warning band sits directly below the rejection.\n   - Set `ownerDto.setCapacityWarning(...)` in `toOwnerDtoWithDerivedFields`, which both the create and single-owner GET paths flow through \u2014 so the flag is populated identically wherever an owner is returned.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` (fill a fresh city to 40, then the next owner reports `capacityWarning: true`) passes, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
